><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14b: yes there were some practical reflections on the outcomes of the study</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="1" rect="595.276000,552.620000,779.276000,644.620000"
/></highlight
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20251014094853+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="8cf35e43-1b6c-406a-9fa6-6b04006c138b" date="D:20251014094853+10'00'" name="e58adc5e-b729-4268-9873-9fc61ebfa6fd" icon="Comment" page="1" rect="57.352100,621.092000,81.352100,645.092000" subject="Sticky Note" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>The evidence is equivocal whether compression garments&#xD;improve physical performance. Furthermore, a&#xD;range of measures (e.g. rating of perceived exertion,&#xD;kinetic and kinematic outputs and cardiorespiratory&#xD;measures) are likely unchanged with their use. However,&#xD;muscle oscillatory properties, perceived muscle soreness&#xD;and localised skin temperature may be affected.&#xD;Despite evidence suggesting there is little benefit of&#xD;wearing compression garments, it is unlikely that they&#xD;harm performance. Additionally, wearing compression&#xD;garments during certain situations (e.g. exercising in&#xD;cold temperatures) may be of benefit.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="1" rect="595.276000,553.092000,779.276000,645.092000"
/></text
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20251014094917+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20251014094937+10'00'" name="e102faa9-02fe-46e8-89ef-45ff932e1e86" page="1" coords="346.238000,623.340000,544.181000,623.340000,346.238000,608.250000,544.181000,608.250000,306.144000,610.840000,544.264000,610.840000,306.144000,595.750000,544.264000,595.750000,306.144000,598.340000,544.369000,598.340000,306.144000,583.250000,544.369000,583.250000,306.144000,585.840000,544.288000,585.840000,306.144000,570.750000,544.288000,570.750000,306.144000,573.340000,369.874000,573.340000,306.144000,558.250000,369.874000,558.250000" rect="305.672000,557.779000,544.840000,623.812000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q3: yes there was previous research on this topic. This article justified as more evidence is needed to change practice</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="1" rect="595.276000,531.340000,779.276000,623.340000"
/></highlight
